\nMeta Description: Track Bitcoin’s drop below $77,000, the $584M liquidation wave, macro risk-off pressure, and the key levels traders should watch next.\nURL Slug: bitcoin-flash-crash-below-77000-liquidation-wave\nCategories: Bitcoin News, Latest News\nPrimary Keyword: Bitcoin flash crash\nSecondary Keywords: crypto liquidation wave, $77K Bitcoin, macro risk-off pressure\n\n# Bitcoin flash crash sends BTC under $77,000 as liquidations hit $584M\n\nBitcoin flash crash price action pushed BTC briefly below $77,000 and reset positioning across the market. Several reports described the move as a flash crash, with one intraday estimate showing about $500 million in long liquidations within an hour and broader 24-hour losses near $584 million.\n\nThe selling spread beyond Bitcoin. Major altcoins fell with it, which made the move look more like a leverage unwind than a project-specific failure. Once $77K broke, forced selling accelerated the decline.\n\nThis looks more like a derivatives flush under macro pressure than a lasting structural break.\n\n## Crypto liquidation wave: What the $77K break shows\n\nThe crypto liquidation wave explains why the move was so violent. Spot selling likely started the slide, but liquidations amplified it once support failed. That is what turns a normal pullback into an air pocket.\n\nCoverage through the session pointed to the same setup. [Startup Fortune](https://startupfortune.com/bitcoin-slides-under-77000-as-macro-storm-hits-crypto/) framed the move as part of a wider macro risk event, while [The Deep Dive](https://thedeepdive.ca/crypto-market-takes-another-hit-as-bitcoin-dips-below-77k-in-monday-flash-crash/) described it as a market-wide flash crash rather than a BTC-only dip.\n\n[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]\n\n### Leverage Was the First Weak Point\n\nThe key number here is not just the low print. It is the speed of the forced unwind. A reported $500 million in long liquidations within an hour suggests traders were already leaning too hard to one side before the break.\n\nThe 24-hour liquidation figure near $584 million adds context. This was not one fast wick that instantly reversed. It was a broader deleveraging event that kept pressure on price after the first flush.\n\n- Long positioning was crowded before the drop.\n- Liquidations accelerated after Bitcoin lost $77K.\n- The move spread across majors instead of staying inside BTC.\n\n### Macro Headlines Turned the Dip Into a Wider Flush\n\nMacro risk-off pressure likely made the move worse. Bitbo linked the drop to Trump’s Iran warning, which fits the pattern of traders cutting exposure when geopolitical headlines hit already weak market structure.\n\nThat matters because crypto often trades like a high-beta risk asset in these windows. When geopolitics and broader sentiment turn at the same time, Bitcoin can lose support faster than crypto-only narratives would suggest.\n\nThis helps explain why the sell-off spread across the market. A macro trigger can start the move, and liquidations can quickly magnify it.\n\n## Key $77K Bitcoin Levels Traders Should Watch Now\n\nThe next move depends less on headlines and more on whether Bitcoin can repair the chart quickly. Traders mainly need to know which levels separate a brief flush from a deeper correction.\n\n[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]\n\n### $77K Needs a Fast Reclaim\n\n\n[Showing lines 2-54 of 99 (50.0KB limit). Use offset=55 to continue.]"}],"details":{"truncation":{"truncated":true,"truncatedBy":"bytes","totalLines":98,"totalBytes":55048,"outputLines":53,"outputBytes":51044,"lastLinePartial":false,"firstLineExceedsLimit":false,"maxLines":2000,"maxBytes":51200}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779083232880},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_sckQhocNCedASdHgeOg19RHv","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"biggest_news_event\": \"Bitcoin briefly fell below $77,000 in a market-wide sell-off that triggered a heavy liquidation cascade across crypto.\",\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Bitcoin flash 