.\",\n    \"Bloomingbit’s headline says Bitcoin briefly fell below $77,000 as $500 million in longs were liquidated in an hour.\",\n    \"Bitbo’s item ties the move to Trump’s Iran warning, suggesting a macro/geopolitical catalyst for the downside.\",\n    \"Startup Fortune describes the move as a macro storm hitting crypto, while thedeepdive and grafa both frame it as a market-wide hit rather than an isolated BTC move.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Today’s cross-feed story is a market-wide Bitcoin downside event centered on BTC briefly falling below $77,000 and forcing a cascade of liquidations across crypto. Bitbo’s RSS item is titled ‘Bitcoin Drops Below $77K on Trump’s Iran Warning,’ which points to a geopolitical shock as the immediate catalyst. Startup Fortune’s item, ‘Bitcoin Slides Under $77,000 as Macro Storm Hits Crypto,’ frames the same move as part of a broader macro-driven risk-off trade. bloomingbit’s headline, ‘Bitcoin Briefly Falls Below $77,000 as $500 Million in Longs Liquidated in an Hour,’ adds the clearest intraday liquidation number and emphasizes how quickly leveraged positions were hit. Yahoo Finance’s ‘Crypto Long Liquidations Hit $584 Million in 24-Hour Sell-Off’ extends that view over a full day and shows the move was not just a brief wick but part of a larger unwind. grafa.com’s ‘Crypto long liquidations reach $584M amid market drop’ independently confirms the same aggregate liquidation scale. thedeepdive.ca’s ‘Crypto Market Takes Another Hit as Bitcoin Dips Below $77K in Monday Flash Crash’ reinforces that this was a broader crypto market shock, not just a BTC-only event. A separate Bitget item says BTC fell below the 77,000 mark and that $160 million was liquidated across the network in one hour, while also noting that DeFi and SocialFi were relatively resilient compared with the rest of the market. Taken together, the feed coverage paints one coherent picture: Bitcoin lost the $77K handle, leverage was flushed quickly, and t